{"answer":"Given LPP: \\\\ Maximize $Z = 3x_1 + 5x_2$ \\\\ Subject to constraints: \\\\ 1) $x_1 + 2x_2 \\le 2000$ \\\\ 2) $x_1 + x_2 \\le 1500$ \\\\ 3) $x_2 \\le 600$ \\\\ 4) $x_1, x_2 \\ge 0$ \\\\ \\\\ **Step 1: Find boundary line intercepts** \\\\ - For $x_1 + 2x_2 = 2000$: Intercepts are $(2000, 0)$ and $(0, 1000)$. \\\\ - For $x_1 + x_2 = 1500$: Intercepts are $(1500, 0)$ and $(0, 1500)$. \\\\ - For $x_2 = 600$: Horizontal line at $x_2 = 600$. \\\\ \\\\ **Step 2: Determine corner points of the feasible region** \\\\ - $O(0, 0)$ \\\\ - $A(1500, 0)$ \\\\ - Intersection of $x_1 + x_2 = 1500$ and $x_2 = 600$: $x_1 + 600 = 1500 \\implies B(900, 600)$ \\\\ - Intersection of $x_1 + 2x_2 = 2000$ and $x_2 = 600$: $x_1 + 2(600) = 2000 \\implies C(800, 600)$ \\\\ - $D(0, 1000)$ -- wait, check if $D(0, 1000)$ satisfies $x_2 \\le 600$ (No). \\\\ Let's check constraints for $x_1 + 2x_2 = 2000$ and $x_1 + x_2 = 1500$: \\\\ Subtracting gives $x_2 = 500$, $x_1 = 1000$, so point $(1000, 500)$. Let's check $x_2 \\le 600$ (Satisfied). \\\\ So corner points are: \\\\ 1. $(0,0)$: $Z = 0$ \\\\ 2. $(1500,0)$: $Z = 3(1500) + 5(0) = 4500$ \\\\ 3. $(1000,500)$: $Z = 3(1000) + 5(500) = 3000 + 2500 = 5500$ \\\\ 4. $(800,600)$: $Z = 3(800) + 5(600) = 2400 + 3000 = 5400$ \\\\ 5. $(0,600)$: $Z = 3(0) + 5(600) = 3000$ \\\\ \\\\ **Conclusion:** Maximum $Z = 5500$ at $(x_1, x_2) = (1000, 500)$.","proTip":"Always evaluate the objective function at every corner point of the bounded feasible region to guarantee finding the true optimum.","videoLinks":[{"title":"graphical method linear programming maximization","url":"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=graphical+method+linear+programming+maximization"},{"title":"solve lpp using graphical method","url":"https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=solve+lpp+using+graphical+method"}]}